				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				136,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Land): Advance Element submodule — command execution notification relay\n\nAdvance the Element submodule pointer to 69826df9, integrating fixes that relay executed command notifications from Mountain to Cocoon so that `vscode.commands.onDidExecuteCommand` callbacks fire inside Node.js extensions.\n\nCocoon replaces the dead `@tauri-apps/api/event`.listen call (which never fires without `window.__TAURI__`) with a subscription to the `commands.executed` Emitter channel, fed by the `$acceptCommandExecuted` Vine notification from Mountain and local command routes in Commands/Namespace.ts for extension-to-extension `executeCommand` calls. The `viewId` dual-key resolution strategy (established for `setHtml`/`postMessage`) is extended to five more webview mutators — `dispose`, `setTitle`, `setIconPath`, `setOptions`, `reveal` — so panel mutations arriving before the workbench mounts the `IOverlayWebview` still reach their target.\n\nMountain dual-emits `$acceptCommandExecuted` over Vine when a command is invoked via `sky://command/execute`, alongside the existing Tauri event that reaches the renderer. The Vine notification is fire-and-forget — failure is non-fatal since renderer-side observers are already notified. The `tauri::Emitter` trait import is added in CreateEffectForRequest/Commands.rs to satisfy the compiler.\n\nExtension `onDidExecuteCommand` hooks now fire correctly, webview panel mutations during mount race conditions resolve via the viewId fallback, and Cocoon's Terminal/Service.ts is marked deprecated pending vertical-split cleanup.",
			"SHA": "dd6c26982b5825f174d7c7b2e1f06477c198093b"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-25T21:39:30Z",
			"File": [
